Package: irtDFI
Title: Dynamic Fit Index Cutoffs for Polytomous Item Response Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
        person("Indriani H.", "Ismail", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "indrianiismail15@gmail.com")
Description: Derives model-specific, simulation-based cutoffs for the
    limited-information fit indices of unidimensional polytomous item
    response models fitted with 'mirt' (Chalmers, 2012): the RMSEA, SRMSR,
    CFI and TLI based on the C2 statistic of Cai and Monroe (2014). Data
    are generated from the fitted model (Level 0) and from versions with
    increasing local dependence (Levels 1 to L), refitted, and cutoffs
    are taken from the resulting sampling distributions, following the
    logic of dynamic fit index cutoffs (McNeish and Wolf, 2023) but for
    item response models rather than factor analysis. The package
    also reports how fixed rules of thumb behave for the same model.
